<title>JAPAN: MOF says to auction 10-year JGBs on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>MOF says to auction 10-year JGBs on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is planning to hold an auction of 10-year Japanese government bonds on Tuesday, a MOF official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Traders said the coupon rate for the JGBs to be offered through the auction will likely be set at 2.6 percent, judging from current market conditions.</p>
<p>The issue amount is likely to be 1.0 trillion yen, they said.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
